%I A401433 #13 Nov 01 2026 16:26:37
%S A401433 1,1,2,5,8,27,39,117,127,348,222,1487
%N A401433 Number of orbits of Aut(F_2) on the subgroups of index n of the free group F_2 of rank 2.
%C A401433 This is equivalent to the number of orbits of Out(F_2) = GL(2,Z) on the A057005(n) conjugacy classes of subgroups of index n of F_2. It is also equivalent to the number of GL(2,Z)-orbits of origamis, i.e., square-tiled surfaces, with n squares.
%D A401433 R. C. Lyndon and P. E. Schupp, Combinatorial Group Theory, Springer, 1977, 25.
%H A401433 Maja Gwozdz, <a href="/A401433/a401433.py.txt">A401433 Python code</a>
%H A401433 Frank Herrlich and Gabriela Schmithüsen, <a href="https://doi.org/10.4171/055-1/19">Dessins d'enfants and origami curves</a>, in Handbook of Teichmüller Theory, Vol. II, Eur. Math. Soc., 2009, 767-809.
%H A401433 Lynne D. James, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/S0195-6698(88)80052-0">Operations on hypermaps, and outer automorphisms</a>, European J. Combin. 9 (1988), 551-560.
%H A401433 Gareth A. Jones and Daniel Pinto, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.disc.2009.12.019">Hypermap operations of finite order</a>, Discrete Math. 310 (2010), 1820-1827.
%H A401433 Karsten Kremer, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5445/IR/1000013203">Invariants of complex and p-adic origami-curves</a>, Dissertation, KIT, 2009.
%H A401433 Shun Kumagai, <a href="https://projecteuclid.org/journals/kodai-mathematical-journal/volume-47/issue-2/Calculation-of-Veech-groups-and-Galois-invariants-of-general-origamis/10.2996/kmj47202.short">Calculation of Veech groups and Galois invariants of general origamis</a>, Kodai Math. J. 47 (2024), 137-161.
%H A401433 Gabriela Schmithüsen, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/10586458.2004.10504555">An algorithm for finding the Veech group of an origami</a>, Experiment. Math. 13 (2004), 459-472.
%H A401433 David Zmiaikou, <a href="https://theses.hal.science/tel-00648120">Origamis and permutation groups</a>, Ph.D. thesis, Paris-Sud University, 2011.
%e A401433 a(4) = 5: the 26 origamis with 4 squares create five orbits, i.e., two of genus 1 (the 6 tori whose lattice of periods has cyclic quotient Z/4, and the 2 X 2 square torus alone), one in the stratum H(2) (9 origamis), and two in H(1,1) (6 and 4 origamis).
%e A401433 a(6) = 27: of the 28 SL(2,Z)-orbits of origamis with 6 squares. Precisely two are mirror images of each other (both in H(4), and with 15 origamis each). They merge into one orbit.
